Event data
----------

data/benchmark/events.jsonl holds public events of Toulouse published on
OpenAgenda (https://openagenda.com), fetched through the OpenAgenda API and
through its mirror on OpenDataSoft, the dataset "Public events - OpenAgenda"
(https://public.opendatasoft.com/explore/dataset/evenements-publics-openagenda/).
`make fetch` and `make process` fetch and write the same kind of data into
data/raw/ and data/processed/, which are not committed.

These events are published under the Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0 of
Etalab (https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/), as
OpenAgenda documents it
(https://doc.openagenda.com/fr/article/des-agendas-en-donnees-ouvertes-opendata-1kv0rno/).

The licensor of an event is the organization of the agenda it was created in,
not OpenAgenda, which hosts and distributes the agendas. Each event of the
file keeps its attribution:

  - agenda_title: the agenda, its licensor;
  - url: its canonical link on OpenAgenda;
  - updated_at: the date of its last update at its source.

The agendas: Bibliothèques de Toulouse; Musée des Augustins; Conservatoire à
rayonnement régional de Toulouse; Musée des arts précieux Paul-Dupuy; SCARE -
Syndicat des Cinémas d'Art, de Répertoire et d'Essai; Shotgun; Le Cratère;
Journées européennes du patrimoine - Occitanie; Quai des savoirs; Monuments
de Toulouse; Théâtre Jules-Julien.

The events were modified: read into a common format, their HTML turned into
text, those outside the city or of another period left out, each event kept
once, the sessions of one activity published as separate events merged, and
the set frozen for the benchmark (reference date: 2026-10-19). The contact
details of the contributors of the agendas are not kept.

This project is not affiliated with OpenAgenda nor with the organizers of the
events, and is not endorsed by them.


Images
------

The images of the events are neither kept nor shown: the events are read
without them, and the application links to the page of each event.


Personal data
-------------

The description of an event may name people (artists, speakers). Their
reuse remains subject to the rules on personal data (GDPR).
